---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="FAQ — Army Pink" description="Answers to common questions about Army Pink — donations, mission, partnerships, the Escape Club, the Perks Program, and resources for survivors.">

  <section class="section faq-section">
    <div class="container faq-container">

      <header class="faq-header reveal-item">
        <span class="overline">FAQ</span>
        <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
        <p class="section-lead">
          A few things people often ask us. If you can't find what you're looking for,
          <a href="/contact">get in touch</a> — we'd love to hear from you.
        </p>
      </header>

      <ul class="faq-list reveal-item">

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">Are donations to Army Pink tax-deductible?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Yes. Army Pink is a fiscally sponsored initiative, operating under the
                umbrella of Charity On Top Foundation, a registered 501(c)(3) nonprofit.
                Donations made to support Army Pink are tax-deductible to the extent
                permitted by law through Charity On Top. Your contributions directly support
                our mission to provide safe transportation and critical resources for
                domestic violence survivors.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">What is Army Pink's mission?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Army Pink is a fiscally sponsored initiative dedicated to supporting
                survivors of domestic violence by providing safe transportation, helping
                them leave abusive situations, and begin rebuilding their lives. With the
                support of our fiscal sponsor, every donation and partnership helps us work
                with allies to create a safer, more hopeful future for those impacted by
                abuse.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">Why is safe transportation crucial for survivors?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Leaving an abusive relationship is often the most dangerous time for a
                survivor. Lack of safe transportation can be a life-threatening barrier,
                preventing individuals from escaping harmful environments. Army Pink
                addresses this critical need by funding transportation to safety.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">What is the Escape Club, and how can I join?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                The Escape Club is a community dedicated to helping survivors reclaim their
                lives and heal. To learn more about how you can join and participate, visit
                our <a href="/give">Escape Club page</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">Who are Army Pink's partners?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Army Pink, fiscally sponsored by Charity On Top, is dedicated to supporting
                survivors of domestic violence by providing safe transportation and helping
                them leave abusive situations. Through partnerships with Peace Over Violence
                and Vedanta, a spiritual holistic retreat, we extend our reach and resources.
                We are actively building additional partnerships to strengthen support and
                create a safer, more hopeful future for survivors.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">How can I support Army Pink's initiatives?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Your donations help us provide essential services, including safe
                transportation for survivors. To contribute to our cause,
                <a href="#" data-donate-panel>make a donation</a> today. You can also
                support Army Pink by volunteering your time — visit our
                <a href="/give">Stand with Survivors</a> page to learn more about
                how to get involved.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">How can my organization become a partner of Army Pink?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                We are always seeking organizations that share our commitment to supporting
                survivors. If your mission aligns with ours and you'd like to make a real
                impact, <a href="/contact">reach out to us</a> and start making a
                difference together.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">What is the Perks Program, and how can I benefit from it?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                The Perks Program gives supporters exclusive discounts, wellness experiences,
                and unique perks. <a href="/give">Join The Escape Club</a> today to
                start enjoying these benefits.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">How does Army Pink ensure transparency in its operations?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                We are committed to transparency and accountability. As a fiscally sponsored
                initiative under Charity On Top Foundation, we work with trusted partners
                and provide clear reporting to ensure that every donation directly supports
                survivors and the services they need to stay safe and rebuild their lives.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

        <li class="faq-item">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span class="faq-question">What resources are available for domestic violence survivors?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>
                Survivors can access various resources, including hotlines, shelters,
                counseling services, and legal assistance. Organizations like Peace Over
                Violence offer emergency services, counseling, legal assistance, and
                advocacy for survivors. Visit our
                <a href="/wellness-portal">Calm Room</a> for more information.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </li>

      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="reveal-item">Still have a question?</h2>
      <p class="reveal-item">We respond to every message within a few business days.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions reveal-item">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Contact us</a>
        <a href="#" class="btn btn-ghost" data-donate-panel>Donate</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
